    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Alexandre - thanks for getting in touch; right now, there&#39;s no way to use a phyloseq object directly with MaAsLin1, and the best bet will be to convert through a tabular file like you described. We&#39;re close to finishing up MaAsLin2, though, and have discussed providing a native interface like you suggest - Himel Mallick and Lauren McIver, the two main researchers on MaAsLin2, are included on the MaAsLin users list (CCed) and will be able to provide more information.<div><br></div><div>Thanks again -</div><div>Curtis</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Thu, Sep 27, 2018 at 3:28 PM Thibodeau Alexandre &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">alexandre...@umontreal.ca</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"FR-CA\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">Greatings!<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">I am Alexandre Thibodeau from the University of Montreal. We are currently doing microbiota analysis (16S amplicon sequencing) in animals in relations to foodborne pathogens and we are using more and more MaAsLin, especially\r\n for your field study where many different variables are at play in our study design.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">I was wondering if MaAsLin could be used from a Phyloseq object. For now, we are currently reworking our OUT/ASV table to make it work but it would be nice if we could simply use it with a Phyloseq object or something\r\n like that.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\">Regards<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-CA\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><span><span style=\"width:390px;min-height:184px\"><img width=\"390\" height=\"184\"></span></span><u></u><b><span style=\"font-size:24.0pt;font-family:&quot;French Script MT&quot;;color:#1e3cf2\">Alexandre\r\n Thibodeau<u></u><u></u></span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#262626\">Agent de recherche</span><b><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-size:24.0pt;font-family:&quot;French Script MT&quot;;color:#1e3cf2\"><u></u><u></u></span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#262626\">Faculté de médecine vétérinaire<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#262626\">3200 rue Sicotte, Saint-Hyacinthe<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#262626\">J2S 2M2, Québec, CANADA<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#262626\">Bureau 1101-10 – pavillon Santé publique<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#262626\">Téléphone: <a href=\"tel:(450)%20773-8521\" value=\"+14507738521\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">(450) 773-8521</a> poste 8242<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#262626\">Télécopieur: <a href=\"tel:(450)%20778-8128\" value=\"+14507788128\" target=\"